Z||000014||rockcrawl||12-21-2000||06:19 PM||||I'd estimate about 100 Fieros at last years Carlisle show. It's not just for Fieros, but there is a portion of the show devoted to Fieros. I started going for the Kitcars, which is how I became a Fiero fanatic in the first place. The # of Fieros in attendance has grown every year it seems. It's definately a worthwile show to attend. <A HREF="http://www.carsatcarlisle.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.carsatcarlisle.com</A>  Import - Kit/Replicar Nationals. I think there is a club that organizes the Fiero part of the show, but I don't know which club. Someone here had posted links to pictures from last years show, but I can't find them now.<P>As for a LV meet, I'm not going to be the one to arrange it, I'm no good at that stuff. I don't mind MR2s showing up.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Phil||12-21-2000||08:48 PM||||The club that handles the Fiero portion of the Carlisle Kitcar show is Mid Atlantic Fiero Owners Association <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieropride.com</A> ||||reg||1
